# Mobile-First Responsive Design

## **Core Principles**

### **Mobile-First Approach**
- **Start with mobile**: Design and develop for mobile screens first (320px+)
- **Progressive enhancement**: Add features and complexity for larger screens
- **Touch-first**: Optimize for touch interactions, not mouse hover
- **Performance**: Prioritize fast loading and smooth interactions

### **Breakpoint Strategy**
```css
/* Mobile First - Default styles for mobile */
.component {
  /* Mobile styles (320px+) */
}

/* Tablet */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .component {
    /* Tablet styles */
  }
}

/* Desktop */
@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .component {
    /* Desktop styles */
  }
}

/* Large Desktop */
@media (min-width: 1280px) {
  .component {
    /* Large desktop styles */
  }
}
```

## **Tailwind CSS Mobile-First Classes**

### **Responsive Utilities**
```typescript
// Mobile-first responsive classes
<div className="
  p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8           // Padding: 16px → 24px → 32px
  text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg  // Text size progression
  grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3  // Grid columns
  flex-col md:flex-row         // Layout direction
  gap-2 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6      // Spacing progression
">
```

### **Layout Patterns**
```typescript
// Card layouts - mobile to desktop
<Card className="
  w-full
  p-4 md:p-6
  rounded-lg md:rounded-xl
  shadow-sm md:shadow-md
">
  <CardHeader className="
    pb-3 md:pb-4
    space-y-1 md:space-y-2
  ">
    <CardTitle className="
      text-lg md:text-xl lg:text-2xl
      font-semibold md:font-bold
    ">
      Title
    </CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
</Card>

// Table responsive pattern
<div className="overflow-x-auto">
  <table className="
    w-full
    text-sm md:text-base
    min-w-[600px]  // Prevent table from being too narrow
  ">
    {/* Table content */}
  </table>
</div>
```

## **Component Responsive Patterns**

### **Navigation & Sidebar**
```typescript
// Mobile: Collapsible sidebar, Desktop: Always visible
<Sidebar 
  collapsible="icon" 
  variant="inset"
  className="
    fixed md:relative
    z-50 md:z-auto
    w-64 md:w-72
  "
>

// Header with mobile menu
<div className="
  flex flex-col md:flex-row
  items-start md:items-center
  justify-between
  gap-4 md:gap-6
  p-4 md:p-6
">
  <div className="w-full md:w-auto">
    <h1 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold">Title</h1>
  </div>
  <div className="flex gap-2 w-full md:w-auto">
    <Button size="sm" className="flex-1 md:flex-none">
      Action
    </Button>
  </div>
</div>
```

### **Form Layouts**
```typescript
// Form fields - stacked on mobile, grid on desktop
<div className="
  space-y-4 md:space-y-6
  grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3
  gap-4 md:gap-6
">
  <FormItem className="
    p-2 md:p-3
    space-y-2 md:space-y-3
  ">
    <FormLabel className="text-sm md:text-base">Label</FormLabel>
    <FormControl>
      <Input className="
        h-9 md:h-10
        text-sm md:text-base
        px-3 md:px-4
      " />
    </FormControl>
  </FormItem>
</div>
```

### **Data Display**
```typescript
// List/Card responsive layout
<div className="
  grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4
  gap-3 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6
  p-4 md:p-6
">

// Table with mobile card fallback
<div className="
  block md:hidden
  space-y-3
">
  {items.map(item => (
    <Card key={item.id} className="p-4">
      {/* Mobile card layout */}
    </Card>
  ))}
</div>

<div className="
  hidden md:block
  overflow-x-auto
">
  <table className="w-full">
    {/* Desktop table layout */}
  </table>
</div>
```

## **Touch & Interaction Design**

### **Touch Targets**
```typescript
// Minimum 44px touch targets
<Button className="
  min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]
  px-4 py-3
  text-sm md:text-base
">

// Icon buttons
<Button size="icon" className="
  h-11 w-11  // Larger than default for better touch
  md:h-9 md:w-9  // Smaller on desktop
">
```

### **Spacing & Padding**
```typescript
// Generous spacing for touch
<div className="
  p-4 md:p-6          // More padding on mobile
  space-y-4 md:space-y-6
  gap-3 md:gap-4
">

// Safe areas for mobile
<div className="
  pt-safe-top pb-safe-bottom
  px-4 md:px-6
">
```

## **Performance Considerations**

### **Image Optimization**
```typescript
// Responsive images
<img 
  className="
    w-full h-auto
    max-w-sm md:max-w-md lg:max-w-lg
    rounded-lg md:rounded-xl
  "
  src={imageUrl}
  alt="Description"
  loading="lazy"
/>
```

### **Conditional Rendering**
```typescript
// Show/hide elements based on screen size
<div className="
  hidden md:block  // Desktop only
  block md:hidden  // Mobile only
">
```

## **Accessibility for Mobile**

### **Focus Management**
```typescript
// Proper focus indicators
<Button className="
  focus-visible:ring-2
  focus-visible:ring-ring
  focus-visible:ring-offset-2
  focus-visible:outline-none
">
```

### **Screen Reader Support**
```typescript
// Proper labeling for mobile
<Button 
  aria-label="Close menu"
  className="md:sr-only"  // Only visible to screen readers on desktop
>
  <XIcon className="h-5 w-5" />
</Button>
```

## **Testing Responsive Design**

### **Viewport Testing**
- Test on actual devices when possible
- Use browser dev tools with custom viewport sizes
- Test both portrait and landscape orientations
- Verify touch interactions work properly

### **Breakpoint Checklist**
- [ ] Mobile (320px - 767px): All content accessible, touch-friendly
- [ ] Tablet (768px - 1023px): Improved layout, more content visible
- [ ] Desktop (1024px+): Full layout, hover states, optimal spacing
- [ ] Large screens (1280px+): Enhanced spacing, larger components